ic></sup><italic>a</italic><sub>MEL-overall</sub><italic>&#x02248;0.027 b</italic><sub>MEL-overall</sub><italic>&#x02248;-0.7836</italic></td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">Nonlethal spread of breast cancer from the primary site in the breast to the lymph nodes</td><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50"><italic>p</italic><sub>BC-to-nodes</sub></td><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50"><italic>L</italic><sub>BC-to-nodes</sub>&#x0003d;the fraction of node positive patients among all patients</td><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">1.75 &#x000d7; 10<sup>&#x02212;8</sup></td><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50"><italic>p</italic>&#x0003d;<italic>aN</italic><sup><italic>b</italic></sup> <italic>a</italic><sub>BC-to-nodes</sub><italic>&#x02248;0.000092b</italic><sub>BC-to-nodes</sub><italic>&#x02248;-0.69251</italic></td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">Lethal spread of breast cancer from the lymph nodes to the periphery</td><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50"><italic>p</italic><sub>BC-from-nodes</sub></td><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50"><italic>L</italic><sub>BC-from-nodes</sub>&#x0003d;6.08&#x00025;, the lethal contribution per positive lymph node</td><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">7.96 &#x000d7; 10<sup>&#x02212;9<sup>a</sup></sup></td><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">Undefined</td></tr></tbody></table><table-wrap-foot><fn id="tbfnote1"><label>a</label><p>The size of nodal metastases was found to have a mean value of 5.3&#x02009;mm (<xref rid="tbl3" ref-type="table">Table 3</xref>). The value shown here for <italic>p</italic><sub>BC-overall</sub> is for a mass of 5&#x02009;mm; for 5.3&#x02009;mm, <italic>p</italic><sub>BC-overall</sub>&#x0003d;7.49 &#x000d7; 10<sup>&#x02212;09</sup>.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><table-wrap id="tbl3" position="float"><label>Table 3</label><caption><p content-type="table-title">Sizes of the invasive breast cancer metastases see